  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Trionfetti. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Trionfetti is a four-player partnership game from the Venice–Padua area, related to Truc and Put. Win two of three tricks per hand; the cutter announces the card ranking (comanda) for each smazzata; first to 20 points wins the game, first to 3 games wins the match.',
    objective: 'Win at least two of three tricks per hand to score 1 point (or more if vagaresto is accepted). First team to 20 points wins the game; first to 3 games wins the match.',
    gameplay: "Play is anticlockwise. Player to dealer's right leads. No requirement to follow suit; each trick is won by the highest card according to the current ranking (comanda). Ties go to the first played of equal cards. Optional vagaresto raises the stake for the hand. Up to 4 hands (smazzata) from the same deck; then new dealer shuffles and new cutter announces ranking.",
    keyRules: [
      'Cutter announces card ranking (comanda) for each smazzata',
      'No follow suit; highest by ranking wins trick',
      '2 of 3 tricks wins the hand',
      '20 points to win game; 3 games to win match',
      'Vagaresto optional stake raise',
